# UPGRADE-13

# No-Cost-First Product Platform

# Self-Hosted Core, Local AI, Free/Open Adapters,

# Product Intelligence, Workflow Builder,

# Notifications, Cost Optimizer and Provider Portability

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-12.

PRIMARY PRODUCT PRINCIPLE:

ZERO-COST CORE FIRST.

A developer must be able to install, run, test and meaningfully use
ZCoder without:

* Stripe account
* paid email provider
* paid object storage
* paid observability service
* paid identity provider
* paid vector database
* cloud KMS
* Kubernetes cluster
* managed PostgreSQL
* paid LLM API
* commercial analytics service
* production GitHub App infrastructure

External paid providers may exist only as OPTIONAL adapters.

Never make paid credentials necessary for:

development
unit tests
integration tests
local onboarding
local agents
workflow execution
usage accounting
dashboards
webhooks
developer API
basic notifications

================================================================
0. VERIFY UPGRADE-12 FIRST
==========================

Run:

git status --short
git log -30 --oneline

python -m pytest -q -ra

python main.py --version
python main.py --help

python -m build
git diff --check

Run the current release gate.

Verify:

TENANCY
RLS
AUTHZ
PUBLIC_API
SDK
WEBHOOKS
USAGE_LEDGER
BILLING_BOUNDARY
SECURITY

Do not expand product functionality if a P0 tenant isolation regression
exists.

================================================================

1. CORRECT SAAS WEB TEST ACCOUNTING
   ================================================================

Upgrade-12 reports Web as an optional skip while also claiming:

WEB_PRODUCT: PASS

Audit this carefully.

Create explicit release profiles:

CORE
SELF_HOSTED
SAAS

Rules:

CORE:
Web may be optional.

SELF_HOSTED:
Web required if bundled.

SAAS:
Web tests mandatory.

A skipped required Web test must not produce:

WEB_PRODUCT = PASS

Fix release evidence accordingly.

================================================================
2. NO-COST CAPABILITY MATRIX
============================

Create:

docs/NO-COST-MATRIX.md

For every subsystem record:

Capability
Built-in/local option
External free option
Paid option
Required?
Offline capable?
Limitations

Cover:

LLM
database
storage
authentication
email
notifications
billing
observability
webhooks
search
embeddings
queue
cache
Git hosting
backup

Every required capability needs a no-cost path.

================================================================
3. PROVIDER PORTABILITY
=======================

Create clean interfaces for all external dependencies.

Target architecture:

ZCoder Domain
│
├── ModelProvider
├── BillingProvider
├── EmailProvider
├── NotificationProvider
├── ObjectStorageProvider
├── SecretProvider
├── IdentityProvider
├── AnalyticsProvider
└── SearchProvider

Domain code must not import commercial SDKs directly.

================================================================
4. LOCAL MODEL PROVIDER
=======================

Make local model execution a first-class path.

Support the existing local-provider architecture where available.

Audit for:

Ollama
OpenAI-compatible local endpoint
other already-supported local gateways

Do NOT invent a new model server if ZCoder already supports one.

Target:

zcoder run "Fix tests" --provider local

must be possible without a paid LLM API.

================================================================
5. MODEL CAPABILITY DISCOVERY
=============================

Local models vary in:

context
tool calling
structured output
vision
thinking
coding quality

Use capability discovery/registry.

Do not assume every OpenAI-compatible endpoint supports every feature.

================================================================
6. LOCAL MODEL FALLBACK
=======================

Allow policy such as:

primary = local
fallback = free/BYO provider

Never automatically fall back to a paid provider unless customer policy
explicitly permits spend.

Introduce:

allow_paid_fallback = false

as safe default for no-cost profile.

================================================================
7. COST CLASSIFICATION
======================

Every provider/runtime should declare:

FREE_LOCAL
FREE_REMOTE
CUSTOMER_KEY
PAID_PLATFORM
UNKNOWN

Routing must never classify an unknown price as free.

================================================================
8. ZERO-COST ROUTING MODE
=========================

Add:

--cost-policy zero

or equivalent.

Behavior:

select only eligible zero-cost providers/runtimes.

If unavailable:

fail clearly

rather than silently sending to a paid model.

================================================================
9. COST CAP
===========

Support:

--max-cost 0

as a real policy.

A zero budget must not be interpreted as:

no limit.

================================================================
10. PROVIDER PRICE REGISTRY
===========================

Keep model cost metadata separate from capabilities.

For provider with unknown pricing:

price status = UNKNOWN

Do not infer free access from HTTP success.

================================================================
11. COST OPTIMIZER
==================

Build routing recommendation layer.

Inputs:

required capability
context size
latency preference
cost policy
data residency
tenant policy
available providers

Output:

recommended provider/model
reason
estimated cost class

Security/residency always override cost.

================================================================
12. COST EXPLAINER
==================

Provide:

zcoder models recommend

or equivalent.

Example:

Task: Python refactor

Recommended:

1. local-code-model
   cost: FREE_LOCAL
   capabilities: tool calling

2. provider X
   cost: CUSTOMER_KEY

Rejected:
provider Y
reason: estimated paid usage not allowed

Do not make quality claims without evidence.

================================================================
13. LOCAL STORAGE
=================

Preserve SQLite/local filesystem mode.

No-cost profile should work with:

SQLite
local artifact directory

PostgreSQL remains optional for production/enterprise.

================================================================
14. OBJECT STORAGE ABSTRACTION
==============================

Implement:

LocalObjectStorage

first.

Operations:

put
get
delete
list metadata
signed/local authorization abstraction

Then external object storage can remain adapters.

================================================================
15. FILESYSTEM SECURITY
=======================

Local object storage must enforce:

tenant/project namespace
path traversal prevention
authorization
size limits

Do not treat local storage as inherently trusted.

================================================================
16. LOCAL BACKUP
================

Provide zero-cost local backup path:

SQLite backup
PostgreSQL pg_dump when PostgreSQL exists
artifact archive
configuration export

Do not call it HA/PITR.

================================================================
17. NO-COST SECRET PROVIDER
===========================

Provide safe built-in options:

environment
permission-restricted local file

Do not put plaintext secrets into SQLite configuration.

Cloud KMS remains optional.

================================================================
18. LOCAL IDENTITY MODE
=======================

Keep secure local/self-hosted authentication.

Do not require commercial SSO.

Possible profile:

single-admin local deployment

plus:

OIDC adapter when external IdP exists.

Never weaken SaaS auth merely to simplify local mode.

================================================================
19. DEV IDENTITY
================

Testing/development should use deterministic fake identity provider.

Production must never accidentally enable fake identity mode.

================================================================
20. LOCAL EMAIL
===============

Notifications must not require paid transactional email.

Implement provider boundary.

No-cost paths:

console/log notification
local SMTP
development mailbox adapter

Email is optional for core product behavior.

================================================================
21. IN-APP NOTIFICATIONS
========================

Create first-class in-app notifications.

Examples:

job complete
approval needed
budget reached
quota warning
GitHub disconnected
webhook failed

This becomes the default zero-cost notification channel.

================================================================
22. NOTIFICATION MODEL
======================

Notification:

id
organization
principal
type
severity
title
message
resource
read_at
created_at

Do not embed secrets/raw provider payloads.

================================================================
23. NOTIFICATION PREFERENCES
============================

Support:

in-app
email
webhook

Default:

in-app enabled

External channels optional.

================================================================
24. NOTIFICATION DEDUPLICATION
==============================

Retries must not create 20 identical alerts.

Use stable event/reference identity.

================================================================
25. LOCAL ANALYTICS
===================

Do not require commercial product analytics.

Create internal aggregated product metrics from PostgreSQL/SQLite where
appropriate.

Examples:

jobs completed
jobs failed
active projects
runtime distribution
usage
cost class

Do not send private code/prompts to external analytics by default.

================================================================
26. ANALYTICS PROVIDER INTERFACE
================================

Optional external analytics must use adapter.

Built-in provider:

LocalAnalyticsProvider

may write privacy-safe product events locally.

================================================================
27. PRIVACY-FIRST DEFAULT
=========================

External product analytics:

OFF by default.

Operational metrics remain separate.

Document exact telemetry.

================================================================
28. OPEN OBSERVABILITY
======================

Continue OpenTelemetry-compatible instrumentation.

Zero-cost stack should work with local/open telemetry endpoints.

Application must not require a hosted observability account.

================================================================
29. WORKFLOW BUILDER DOMAIN
===========================

Create reusable workflow definition.

Example:

Workflow:
id
name
trigger
steps
policy
runtime
validation
budget

Steps could include:

agent
command
validation
approval
GitHub PR
notification

Do not make UI JSON blobs the canonical workflow model.

================================================================
30. WORKFLOW VERSIONING
=======================

A workflow change should create a version/reference.

Running jobs retain the exact workflow version used.

================================================================
31. WORKFLOW TEMPLATES
======================

Ship useful built-in templates:

Fix failing tests
Review PR
Security review
Documentation update
Dependency review
Refactor
CI repair

Templates must be editable/copied.

================================================================
32. ORGANIZATION TEMPLATES
==========================

Allow default:

policies
agent profile
validation
workflow
budget
runtime preference

for newly created projects.

================================================================
33. PROJECT TEMPLATES
=====================

Examples:

Python
Node
Full stack
Library
Docker service

Do not make guesses destructive.

Detection should recommend, not silently overwrite project config.

================================================================
34. WORKFLOW EXECUTION
======================

Reuse existing durable job engine.

Workflow builder should compile into:

Job / Plan / Steps

not create a second execution engine.

================================================================
35. WORKFLOW VALIDATION
=======================

Before saving/running:

validate:

cycles
unsupported step
missing runtime
invalid policy
budget contradiction
unavailable provider

Fail early.

================================================================
36. WORKFLOW DRY RUN
====================

Support:

workflow dry-run

Show:

steps
runtime
provider
tools
approvals
estimated cost class
external mutations

No execution.

================================================================
37. WORKFLOW TRIGGERS
=====================

No-cost triggers:

manual
API
GitHub webhook
schedule

Do not require external workflow SaaS.

