65. TEAM COLLABORATION
======================

Build no-cost collaboration features:

job comments
mentions
approval requests
activity stream

No Slack/Teams dependency.

================================================================
66. COMMENTS
============

Comment model:

tenant scoped
resource scoped
actor
timestamp
edited marker

Sanitize rendered content.

================================================================
67. MENTIONS
============

Mentions trigger in-app notifications.

Email remains optional.

================================================================
68. ACTIVITY FEED
=================

Use existing audit/domain events where appropriate.

Do not duplicate every event into another uncontrolled data store.

================================================================
69. APPROVAL INBOX
==================

Provide consolidated view:

job
requested action
risk
requesting agent
age

No external workflow product required.

================================================================
70. SAVED VIEWS
===============

Allow locally stored dashboard filters.

Examples:

My approvals
Failed jobs
Zero-cost jobs
Paid jobs
Budget warnings

================================================================
71. SEARCH
==========

Start with database-backed bounded search.

Do not require Elasticsearch/OpenSearch/vector DB initially.

Upgrade only if scale proves need.

================================================================
72. FULL-TEXT SEARCH
====================

If PostgreSQL is present, evaluate native full-text functionality where
appropriate.

SQLite local mode can offer simpler search.

Keep interface portable.

================================================================
73. VECTOR SEARCH
=================

Do NOT add vector DB merely because this is an AI product.

Only introduce if a real feature requires semantic retrieval.

================================================================
74. LOCAL CACHE
===============

Do not require Redis.

Built-in process/cache or DB-backed strategy may be adequate.

If Redis adapter exists:

optional only.

================================================================
75. QUEUE
=========

Do not require Kafka/RabbitMQ/Redis queue.

Use PostgreSQL durable queue/control-plane architecture already present
for production.

SQLite local execution remains local.

================================================================
76. NO-COST INFRASTRUCTURE PROFILE
==================================

Define:

zcoder profile local-free

Equivalent configuration:

storage: sqlite
artifacts: local
billing: fake/disabled
analytics: local
notifications: in_app
models: local/BYO only
telemetry: local/disabled
email: disabled
external_paid_fallback: false

================================================================
77. SELF-HOSTED FREE PROFILE
============================

Define:

storage: postgres optional
artifacts: local
billing: disabled/fake
models: local/BYO
web: enabled
API: enabled

No license server dependency for core operation unless product
requirements explicitly require it.

================================================================
78. FREE PROFILE FAIL-SAFE
==========================

If a paid-only feature is requested:

respond clearly:

PAID_PROVIDER_REQUIRED

Do not automatically enable a paid adapter.

================================================================
79. PROVIDER BUDGET POLICY
==========================

Add global/tenant policy:

paid_providers:
allowed: false

or equivalent.

Enforce at runtime layer.

================================================================
80. NETWORK POLICY
==================

Zero-cost local mode should not call unknown external services
automatically.

Document every outbound integration.

================================================================
81. OFFLINE MODE
================

Introduce:

--offline

where feasible.

Offline mode disables:

cloud provider calls
remote telemetry
external billing
external webhooks

Local models/local Git operations remain available.

Do not promise full functionality where internet is fundamentally needed.

================================================================
82. OFFLINE TEST
================

Run process with network disabled/mocked.

Verify core:

CLI
local provider configuration
workflow engine
SQLite
dashboard startup
job persistence

does not require external SaaS.

================================================================
83. FREE-FIRST ONBOARDING
=========================

First-run experience:

Choose mode:

1. Local Free
2. Self-Hosted
3. Cloud/BYO
4. Commercial SaaS

Default should not force credit card or paid provider.

