## 27. Final Verdict

Do not say:

ZERO COST

if normal operation silently depends on a paid service.

Correct terminology is:

NO-COST CORE

only when an actual user can install and complete a meaningful workflow
without providing commercial provider credentials.

The highest priority is:

useful software first,
paid integrations second.
